  "bio_summary": "Parul Chaudhary is an Indian long-distance runner specializing in the 3000m steeplechase and 5000m events. Born in Iklauta village, Uttar Pradesh, she began her athletic career running barefoot and has since become one of India's most accomplished female distance runners. She holds multiple national records and has achieved significant international success, including gold and silver medals at the Asian Games and Asian Athletics Championships. Chaudhary also represented India at the Paris 2024 Olympics.",
